<EXPERIMENT_PACKAGE><EXPERIMENT accession="SRX26377937" alias="GSM8571270_r1"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRX26377937</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM8571270_r1</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>GSM8571270: PMA-stimulated THP1 cells, 1h, vehicle (DMSO:EtOH), ATAC-seq, replicate 1; Homo sapiens; ATAC-seq</TITLE><STUDY_REF accession="SRP468605"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP468605</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject">PRJNA1032482</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></STUDY_REF><DESIGN><DESIGN_DESCRIPTION/><SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR accession="SRS22901768"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS22901768</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM8571270</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_NAME>GSM8571270</LIBRARY_NAME><LIBRARY_STRATEGY>ATAC-seq</LIBRARY_STRATEGY><LIBRARY_SOURCE>GENOMIC</LIBRARY_SOURCE><LIBRARY_SELECTION>other</LIBRARY_SELECTION><LIBRARY_LAYOUT><SINGLE/></LIBRARY_LAYOUT><LIBRARY_CONSTRUCTION_PROTOCOL>Cells were counted and 50,000 cells were collected in ice-cold PBS. The nuclei were isolated with ATAC lysis buffer (10 mM Tris–HCl pH 7.4, 10 mM NaCl, 3 mM MgCl2, and 0.1% IGEPAL). Tagmentation of the nuclei was performed using the Tagment DNA TDE1 Enzyme and Buffer Kits (Illumina). Indexing was performed using Nextera DNA library preparation kit (Illumina). DNA was purified with NucleoSpin Gel and PCR Clean-up Kit (Macherey-Nagel). Indexed DNA was amplified for nine PCR cycles with Kapa Hifi Hot Start Kit (Kapa Biosystems). Amplified libraries were purified again with NucleoSpin Gel and PCR Clean-up Kit (Macherey-Nagel). Indexed libraries were prepared from tagmented DNA, using Nextera DNA library preparation kit (Illumina)</LIBRARY_CONSTRUCTION_PROTOCOL></LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR></DESIGN><PLATFORM><ILLUMINA><INSTRUMENT_MODEL>NextSeq 500</INSTRUMENT_MODEL></ILLUMINA></PLATFORM></EXPERIMENT><SUBMISSION lab_name="" center_name="UNIVERSITY OF DEBRECEN" accession="SRA1991602" alias="SUB14790628"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRA1991602</PRIMARY_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="UNIVERSITY OF DEBRECEN">SUB14790628</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SUBMISSION><Organization type="institute"><Name>University of Debrecen</Name><Contact email="lnagy@jhmi.edu"><Address><Street>Egyetem ter 1.</Street><City>Debrecen</City><Country>Hungary</Country></Address><Name><First>Laszlo</First><Last>Nagy</Last></Name></Contact></Organization><STUDY center_name="GEO" alias="GSE246307" accession="SRP468605"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP468605</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject" label="primary">PRJNA1032482</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSE246307</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_TITLE>Genomic regions occupied by both RARa and VDR are involved in the convergence and cooperation of retinoid and vitamin D signaling pathways.</STUDY_TITLE><STUDY_TYPE existing_study_type="Other"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>In this study, the retinoid and vitamin D pathways were investigated in PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells treated with or without the RARa agonist, AM580, and/or the VDR agonist, 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 (1,25-vitD or calcitriol), using global approaches. Binding regions of RARa and VDR were determined in PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells using chromatin immunoprecipitation coupled with high-throughput sequencing (ChIP-seq). The gene sets regulated by AM580 and/or 1,25-vitD were identified by RNA-sequencing (RNA-seq). The activity of the regulatory regions was determined by MED1 (a subunit of the Mediator complex) ChIP-seq and chromatin openness was measured using assay for transposase-accessible chromatin with sequencing (ATAC-seq). Overall design: THP-1 cells were stimulated with 20 nM PMA for 16 hours. PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells were treated with vehicle (DMSO:EtOH) or 100 nM AM580 for 1 hour. Two replicates for each treatment condition were analyzed for ATAC-seq.</STUDY_ABSTRACT><CENTER_PROJECT_NAME>GSE246307</CENTER_PROJECT_NAME></DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>pubmed</DB><ID>40167329</ID></XREF_LINK></STUDY_LINK></STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_ATTRIBUTES><STUDY_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>parent_bioproject</TAG><VALUE>PRJNA1032473</VALUE></STUDY_ATTRIBUTE></STUDY_ATTRIBUTES></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="GSM8571270" accession="SRS22901768"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS22901768</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN44280626</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM8571270</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>PMA-stimulated THP1 cells, 1h, vehicle (DMSO:EtOH), ATAC-seq, replicate 1</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>9606</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>Homo sapiens</SCIENTIFIC_NAME></SAMPLE_NAME><SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>bioproject</DB><ID>1032482</ID><LABEL>PRJNA1032482</LABEL></XREF_LINK></SAMPLE_LINK></SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>source_name</TAG><VALUE>THP-1 human leukemia monocytic cell line</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>cell line</TAG><VALUE>THP-1 human leukemia monocytic cell line</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>stimulation</TAG><VALUE>phorbol-12-myristate-13-acetate (PMA) for 16h</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>treatment</TAG><VALUE>vehicle (DMSO:EtOH)</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>time</TAG><VALUE>1h</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>genotype</TAG><VALUE>wt</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>geo_loc_name</TAG><VALUE>missing</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>collection_date</TAG><VALUE>missing</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES></SAMPLE><Pool><Member member_name="" accession="SRS22901768" sample_name="GSM8571270" sample_title="PMA-stimulated THP1 cells, 1h, vehicle (DMSO:EtOH), ATAC-seq, replicate 1" spots="31441064" bases="2389520864" tax_id="9606" organism="Homo sapiens"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS22901768</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN44280626</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM8571270</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></Member></Pool><RUN_SET runs="1" bases="2389520864" spo